## VACUITY READ — all 31 final theorems (CX-P12 self-read, 2026-10-20)
Read the complete final theorem statements and proof modules directly. This is the lane's own read, not an independent second reader. All landed declarations remain byte-identical. No arbitrary graph is silently restricted by a new premise on a landed theorem. Every new conclusion's disjuncts checked; the only explicit conclusion disjunction is holds_append's two provenance alternatives, addressed below. Existential witnesses are bounded carrier members, graph edges or actual named result constructors, not an unbounded collision predicate.
1. holds_product: Boolean image of full positive/negative Cartesian product equals BOTH leaf images. No disjunct; neither required polynomial is omitted; concrete direct-output teeth refute dropping either polarity.
2. holds_append: explicit RHS disjuncts Holds w p and Holds w q; arbitrary p/q/w and no premises force neither branch individually. Empty p with live q and vice versa need opposite branches. The union interpretation is substantive, not an unrelated escape disjunct.
3. mem_edges: flattened finite edge enumeration equals actual body reference membership; no disjunction. Namespace coverage matters and is mutated.
4. validate_iff: actual executable scan equals independent strict descent for every body reference; no disjunction and no successful-validator premise defines Ranked. Positive chain and negative badWitness inhabit both outcomes.
5. depends_rank: a nonempty dependency path strictly descends rank; no disjunction. Path transitivity is proved, not assumed. Valid chain inhabits the premises.
6. cycles_not_ranked: a real self-returning dependency path excludes every rank certificate; no disjunction. self_dependency and mutual_dependency inhabit the premise; not an impossible cycle-and-Ranked antecedent.
7. expand_sound: sound meanings for referenced holes lift through arbitrary expressions to independent derivation trees; no disjunction in conclusion. It constructs tokens/alternatives/joints, not a compiler-success alias.
8. unroll_sound: any successful finite approximation yields an independent finite derivation, even without ranks; no disjunction. Fuel zero's empty premise is one base case, not the whole theorem; positive chain expansions are nonempty.
9. expand_complete: completeness on actual referenced holes lifts through expression structure; no disjunction in conclusion. Requires real Derives constructors; does not assume expanded Holds as the target premise.
10. unroll_complete: independently Ranked and sufficient rank bound imply completeness for arbitrary derivations; no disjunction. Rank is about edges, not assumed derivation height. Positive chain inhabits the premise; this is a NEW adapter helper only.
11. adapt_correct: returned polynomial truth iff independent Derives, at every token world; no disjunction. Success supplies the executed certificate, not the desired semantics. chain_exact inhabits success. Generic candidate composition consumes it.
12. adapt_acyclic: actual success excludes a nonempty return path at ANY hole, including undemanded ones; no disjunction. Finite namespace/root exists on positive chain; not an empty domain trick.
13. cycle_refused: actual self-returning path yields an actual .error reason for any root; existential ranges over named Refusal constructors, not an arbitrary predicate. Cycle examples inhabit the premise.
14. refusal_explained: every returned refusal names an actual syntactic edge, failing rank inequality and exact conditional endpoint reason; no disjunction. Conditional chooses reason classification rather than permitting an escape. Self vs bad-rank examples exercise both classes.
15. ranked_accepted: independent valid rank evidence makes the executed adapter succeed; no disjunction. Completeness of checking, not a premise asserting the same returned tag.
16. expand_congr: equality of lookups on actual references suffices for exact expression output; no disjunction. Reads only those syntactic references, not an assumed equality on the result.
17. unroll_stable: two adequate depths produce exactly the same lists, preserving order/multiplicity; no disjunction. Distinct k/m allowed; no assumed equality of the depths or outputs.
18. unroll_equation: output at each hole equals full expansion against every dependency's own adequate output; no disjunction. Uses strict descent/stabilization to discharge actual dependencies, not a cyclic equation assumed as a premise.
19. chain_stratifies: arbitrary leaf polynomials admit this concrete two-hole rank witness; no disjunction or antecedent. Positive witness for general Ranked-based results.
20. chain_exact: arbitrary leaf polynomials produce their direct Cartesian product through adapt, exactly; no disjunction or antecedent. Captures joint dependency rather than erasing it.
21. chain_candidates: actual consumer and dependency candidate judges BOTH verify iff the adapter's independent derivation exists. No disjunction; candidates drawn from explicit supplied lists; no claim beyond the landed fixed-environment leaf scope. Uses landed provenance_iff directly, no alias theorem counted as new content.
22. two_hole_direct: exact nonempty two-alternative polynomial with both supports/blockers; no disjunction. Product and depth mutations fail it.
23. self_refused_by_name: seeded self-dependent hole emits fixedPointDependency 0, not success or a generic tag; no disjunction. The real bypass mutation fails this statement and prints silent-drop success.
24. unchecked_self_drops: internal unroll of that invalid graph equals the seed; no disjunction. Deliberate counterexample explaining why raw unroll is not the certified adapter; not a claim of acceptable fixed-point semantics.
25. mutual_refused_by_edge: two-hole cycle emits its actual first nondecreasing edge 0→1; no disjunction. Does not label every failed ranking as proof of a cycle.
26. undemanded_cycle_refused: querying hole0 still refuses hole1's self-reference; no disjunction. Whole-graph coverage mutation fails it.
27. zero_masked_cycle_refused: zero leaf product does not justify erasing a self-reference; no disjunction. Joint reference-coverage mutation fails it.
28. bad_rank_witness_refused: acyclic graph with equal supplied ranks returns rankNotDecreasing 1 0; no disjunction. It tests the witness, not acyclicity inference.
29. bad_witness_has_valid_replacement: identical chain bodies with correct rank evidence succeed; no disjunction. Explicit contrasting positive instance, not a general new algorithm claim; a concrete specialization of chain_exact.
30. self_dependency: explicit edge inhabits Depends selfDependent 0 0; no disjunction. Supplies the generic boundary's nonempty-cycle premise.
31. mutual_dependency: two actual edges form a nonempty 0→1→0 path; no disjunction. Indirect-cycle premise is demonstrably inhabited.

