Beyond these basic well-formedness conditions, a DAIG’s
structure must also properly encode an abstract interpretation computation over an underlying program. Given a
program’s CFG and an abstract interpreter interface (as defined in Section 3), there are three general cases shown in
Fig. 7 to consider when examining a corresponding DAIG.
The key property is that demand-driven query evaluation
and incremental edits will evolve the DAIG but preserve the
